1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,220
Hi everyone welcome back to my channel.
大家好，欢迎回到我的频道。

2
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:10,810
So for this journal entry episode eight we're going to be talking about why having no friends is completely okay.
这期日记是第八集，我们要聊聊，为什么没有朋友也完全没关系。

3
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:16,259
I'm kind of shocked that I haven't talked about because as you guys can see I do a lot of things by myself.
我有点惊讶自己之前居然没聊过，因为你们也看得出来，我经常一个人做很多事情。

4
00:00:16,259 --> 00:00:21,899
I've always had trouble keeping friends long term this can go into a lot of issues of mine.
我一直不太擅长长期维持友谊。这可能涉及我自己的很多问题。

5
00:00:21,899 --> 00:00:24,540
And as a kid I've always been extremely insecure.
小时候，我一直非常缺乏安全感。

6
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:28,739
Because I didn't have you know a lot of friends that I had like really low self esteem.
因为我没有很多朋友，我那时的自尊和自我评价都很低。

7
00:00:28,739 --> 00:00:33,120
Ever since I was a kid I did everything by myself but it was always kind of like I had to.
从小时候起，我就总是自己做所有事情，但那种感觉一直像是不得不这样。

8
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:38,570
I didn't really learn to enjoy doing things by myself.
我并没有真正学会享受一个人做事情。

9
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:43,970
As a kid I've always been envious of girls who are friends with each other you know girls who have lots of friends.
小时候，我总羡慕那些彼此是朋友的女孩，就是那些有很多朋友的女孩。

10
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:50,940
And I always wanted to be like that but as I gotten older I realized how having no friends is really okay it really is.
我一直想像她们那样，但随着年龄增长，我发现，没有朋友也真的可以，真的。

11
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:56,520
When you are alone you figure out a lot of things that you've never really known about yourself.
一个人的时候，你会发现很多以前并不真正了解的自己。

12
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:59,999
Because sometimes when you're in group setting a lot of us tend to just like go with the flow.
因为有时候，在一群人中，我们很多人容易顺着大家的安排走。

13
00:00:59,999 --> 00:01:04,499
You go with what your friends want I want to do this because I just want to enjoy their company which is completely fine.
你跟着朋友想做的事情走；我想做这件事，是因为我想和他们待在一起，这当然没问题。

14
00:01:04,499 --> 00:01:09,300
But you don't realize what you want you like this activity because you guys are doing it together right.
但你可能并不清楚自己想要什么。你喜欢这项活动，是因为大家一起做，对吧？

15
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:14,580
You have your friends company you like their company so as you like this activity that doesn't mean you like this activity.
你有朋友作伴，你喜欢他们的陪伴，于是你也喜欢这项活动；但这不代表你本身就喜欢它。

16
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:19,679
When you have no friends to hang out with all you have is yourself so you really try to do things that you enjoy right.
当没有朋友可以一起出去时，只有你自己，你就会真正尝试去做自己喜欢的事情，对吧？

17
00:01:19,679 --> 00:01:23,750
It's very obvious like you know we all want friends so it's very very normal to feel lonely.
这很明显，你知道，我们都想有朋友，所以感到孤独是非常正常的。

18
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:28,760
Because sometimes I feel like when we feel lonely it's like you feel bad about it you're like.
因为我觉得，有时我们感到孤独，又会为这种感受本身而难受，心里就会想……

19
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:35,580
But you need to understand that is very very normal it is normal to feel lonely it is normal to want company from people.
但你要知道，这真的很正常。感到孤独很正常，想有人陪伴也很正常。

20
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:41,150
And start pushing the thought away I tell myself that this is normal I'm a human being I shouldn't want to socialize with people.
接下来字幕衔接有疑点：她说会告诉自己“这很正常，我是人”。字幕随后写成“我不应该想与人社交”，是否有否定词误识，待听辨。

21
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:46,320
Friendships can also make you feel lonely just because you're in a group of people doesn't mean that you would feel included.
友谊也可能让你感到孤独。身处一群人中，并不代表就会觉得自己被接纳，对吧？

22
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:48,899
Right somehow you're in a group of people feel like an outcast.
有时候，你就在一群人中，却觉得自己像个局外人。

23
00:01:48,899 --> 00:01:53,160
You just feel like oh my god like I feel like nobody here really gives two shits about me.
你会想：天哪，我觉得这里根本没有人在乎我。

24
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:57,899
Like I said I'm just here just to be here I just want the company of others even though I'm not really enjoying their company.
像我说的，我只是为了在场而在场，只是想有人陪着，尽管我并不真正享受和他们相处。

25
00:01:57,899 --> 00:02:01,259
So would you rather be feeling lonely by yourself or feeling lonely in a group.
所以，你更愿意一个人感到孤独，还是在一群人中感到孤独？

26
00:02:01,259 --> 00:02:05,280
Personally I would rather feel lonely by myself like what's the point hang out with people if you feel lonely.
就我个人而言，我宁愿一个人孤独。如果和别人一起还是孤独，那一起出去又有什么意义呢？

27
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:10,140
When you're with friends you can become so fixated on them you can become so focused on them.
和朋友在一起时，你可能会变得特别执着于他们，把注意力全放在他们身上。

28
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:14,389
That you don't really care about what you want you don't care about the goals you have.
以至于你不再真正关心自己想要什么，也不再关心自己的目标。

29
00:02:14,399 --> 00:02:17,399
Because some of us just want to hold on to that song want to hold on to these friends.
因为有些人只想紧紧抓住这些朋友。前面的 that song 与语境不协调，具体所指待听辨。

30
00:02:17,399 --> 00:02:22,070
Because you just feel you've been alone for so long what if they leave me what do they leave me for someone else whether I'm not good enough.
因为你觉得自己已经孤单很久了：万一他们离开我呢？如果他们选了别人呢？是不是我不够好？后两处字幕识别有疑点。

31
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:24,500
And I don't blame you because you know we all want friends.
我不怪你，因为我们都想有朋友。

32
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:29,700
Sometimes you might even lose your passions and your goals you might set that aside.
有时你甚至可能把热情和目标都丢到一边，暂时搁置下来。

33
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:36,780
It's like a thing that you don't even realize and that is not to say like this is a friend's fault it's our fault I'm not encouraging youtube boyfriend.
这有时是你自己都没察觉的事。她接着说，这不是朋友的错，而是自己的问题；后一句被识别成 youtube boyfriend，无法可靠翻译。

34
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:41,940
When you're just completely alone with no friends I feel like there's a certain breakthrough that you probably never have.
当完全独处、没有朋友时，我觉得你可能会经历某种此前没有过的突破。

35
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:46,259
I mean of course it gets dark sometimes but also it can be a breakthrough.
当然，有时也会很难熬，但也可能带来突破。

36
00:02:46,259 --> 00:02:49,740
You realize how capable you are to do absolutely everything by yourself.
你会发现，原来自己有能力独立做这么多事情。

37
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:53,820
Once you have this mindset even when you get back into friend groups you will still have this mindset.
一旦有了这种心态，就算后来回到朋友群体中，你也依然会保有它。

38
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:56,810
I personally don't think it can be taken away once you have this breakthrough.
我个人觉得，一旦有了这种突破，这种认识就不会被拿走。

39
00:02:56,820 --> 00:02:59,630
When you have no friends you realize that I have to do everything for myself.
没有朋友时，你会意识到，很多事得靠自己来做。

40
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:06,300
Sometimes these things is just like you have to just do it you have so much fear you're like oh my god I cannot do this I have to do this with someone else but you can literally.
有些事情就是得迈出那一步。你会很害怕，觉得“我不行，必须有人陪我”，但她说，你其实可以。

41
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:10,140
Sometimes we just overthink but the things that when we think so much about it it's a waste of energy.
有时我们想得太多；一件事反复想来想去，其实很消耗精力。

42
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:12,780
It's literally a waste of energy to be anxious about a 24/7.
她说，整天为它焦虑很耗精力；字幕中的 about a 与后面的 24 7 衔接含混，待听辨。

43
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:16,370
Just do it because trust me when you actually do the thing it's not as scary as you think.
试试看吧，因为相信我，真去做的时候，它往往没有你想的那么可怕——这是她的感受。
